# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build / run output. None of this belongs in the repo, and a stray
# `git add <dir>` that sweeps it in makes pushes crawl (486MB of CIFAR under
# content/data alone). Keep these rules ahead of any broad `git add`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Dataset downloads, re-fetched by the notebooks on demand
content/data/
/data/

# Training/run artifacts written by example code
content/outputs/
content/logs/
/logs/
jpgs/

# Local scratch renders and packaging metadata
content/_site_test/
src/*.egg-info/

# Loose screenshots dropped in the repo root while iterating on the design.
# Anything a page actually uses lives under content/assets/ or content/**/img/.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.webp

# content/assets/ is a staging area Quarto copies FROM, and every file a page
# actually uses is already committed on the other side, under docs/. Tracking
# the source copies too would duplicate ~45MB of gifs/pdfs in a repo whose
# history is already large, so the whole staging dir stays ignored -- except
# the handful of hand-authored SVGs that were tracked before this rule.
content/assets/
!content/assets/anl_logos/
!content/assets/linear-net-with-weights.svg

# Per-page rendered figure dirs mirrored into the source tree (docs/ has them)
content/**/index_files/

# Python bytecode and packaging strays
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Re-running a diagram cell writes a fresh `<name>1/`, `<name>2/`, ... beside
# the real one. Only the unnumbered dir is referenced by a page; the numbered
# copies are duplicates of it.
content/**/img/*[0-9]/

# Scratch left behind by the MPI examples
content/mpi_pi.py.[0-9]*
content/test-index.html
/hostfile
content/hostfile

# Image/data payloads for the two notebooks parked out of the render (see the
# `!...index.ipynb` excludes in content/_quarto.yml). The notebooks themselves
# stay tracked; these are just their unused attachments.
content/01-neural-networks/2-advanced/images/
content/01-neural-networks/2-advanced/data/
content/01-neural-networks/1-mnist-ipynb/images/

# One-off probe render
content/01-neural-networks/2-conv-nets/_cwdprobe.html
content/01-neural-networks/2-conv-nets/_cwdprobe_files/

# Datasets/scratch pulled into content/ by example code
content/input.txt
content/slimmed_realestate_data.csv
content/02-llms/Untitled.ipynb
